KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member typedef mem-init survives: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A computed default template argument containing an alias whose RHS is
a clang builtin trait type (add_rref_t<T> = __add_rvalue_reference(T))
breaks the member-typedef mem-initializer of a class instantiated
later: "symbol '__base' is unknown".  Root of the
silent-statement-dropping family (cpp20_optional_base_alias_unknown,
cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx, cpp17_optional_requires_ctor_pair; libc++
std::optional's __optional_move_assign_base machinery).
Without the alias inside the default the same shape converts.
clang++/valgrind clean (clang-only builtin; g++ n/a).
